Let matrix be a list of 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, and 1.
Let rows be 3.
Let columns be 3.
Let last row be rows minus 1.
Let last column be columns minus 1.
Let rowmarks be an empty list of whole numbers.
Let colmarks be an empty list of whole numbers.
For every row from 0 to last row.
For every column from 0 to last column.
If item (row times columns plus column) of matrix is 0, append row to rowmarks.
If item (row times columns plus column) of matrix is 0, append column to colmarks.

For each row in rowmarks.
For every column from 0 to last column.
Set item (row times columns plus column) of matrix to 0.

For each column in colmarks.
For every row from 0 to last row.
Set item (row times columns plus column) of matrix to 0.

For each value in matrix, print value.
